<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manhattan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manhattan is an island at the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudson-river">Hudson River</a> and the central borough of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> City. Inhabited by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lenape">Lenape</a>, it was bought from them in 1626, by tradition for goods worth 60 guilders, by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-minuit">Peter Minuit</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-west-india-company">Dutch West India Company</a>, and became the site of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-amsterdam">New Amsterdam</a>, capital of New Netherland. Taken by the English in 1664, it grew into the commercial and financial heart of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manhattan.jpg" alt="Manhattan" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dllu · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_Empire_State_Building_from_Rockefeller_Center_New_York_City_dllu_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
